Let $f(x) = x^3 - 3x^2 + 3.$  Then the given recursion becomes $a_{n + 1} = f(a_n).$  Note that
\[f(x) - x = x^3 - 3x^2 + 3 - x = (x - 1)^3 - 1.\]Hence, $f(x) = x$ if and only if $(x - 1)^3 = 1,$ which means $x = 2.$

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

real func (real x) {
  return(x^3 - 3*x^2 + 3);
}

draw(graph(func,-1.5,3.5));
draw((-1.5,-1.5)--(3.5,3.5),dashed);
draw((-1.5,0)--(3.5,0));
draw((0,-1.5)--(0,3.5));

label("$y = f(x)$", (3.5,func(3.5)), E);
label("$y = x$", (3.5,3.5), E, UnFill);

dot("$2$", (2,2), NE);
[/asy]

If $a_{2007} = a_0,$ then
\[a_0 = a_{2007} = f(a_{2006}) = f(f(a_{2005})) = \dots = f^{2007}(a_0),\]where $f^{2007}$ denotes the function $f$ composed with itself 2007 times.

Suppose $a_0 \neq 2.$  If $a_0 < 2,$ then $f(a_0) < a_0.$  If $a_0 > 2,$ then $f(a_0) > a_0.$  In either case, $f^{2007}(a_0) \neq a_0.$

Therefore, the only possible value of $a_0$ is $\boxed{1}.$  We can check that this works, since the sequence becomes constant.
TERMINATE

